#  Fake News Detection using Fine-Tuned DistilBERT

##  Project Overview

This project develops a **Fake News Detection** system using a fine-tuned **DistilBERT** transformer model. The objective is to classify news articles as **Fake** or **Real** using Natural Language Processing (NLP) and deep learning techniques.

The project compares traditional machine learning approaches with transformer-based models to evaluate the effectiveness of transfer learning for text classification.

---

##  Project Objectives

- Build a binary text classification model for fake news detection.
- Compare traditional machine learning models with transformer-based models.
- Fine-tune a pre-trained DistilBERT model for improved performance.
- Evaluate model performance using multiple classification metrics.

---

##  Dataset

- **Source:** Hugging Face Fake News Dataset
- **Task:** Binary Text Classification
- **Classes:**
  - Fake News
  - Real News

---

##  Models Compared

- TF-IDF + Logistic Regression
- TF-IDF + Multinomial Naive Bayes
- Frozen DistilBERT + Logistic Regression
- Fine-Tuned DistilBERT

---

##  Model Performance

| Model | Accuracy |
|-------|----------|
| TF-IDF + Logistic Regression | **96.40%** |
| TF-IDF + Naive Bayes | **93.35%** |
| Frozen DistilBERT | **97.50%** |
| **Fine-Tuned DistilBERT** | **98.85%** |

The Fine-Tuned DistilBERT model achieved the highest performance, demonstrating the effectiveness of transformer-based transfer learning for fake news classification.

